{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_276f6a53f22536c65aa73f2270fdabd2966b5b977fa02760bb63035850c9bbeb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"dyad-sh/dyad@0c8403662504 snapshot 73f45ce23df314b3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_055ede43501dbc935d59e8f0ded083abcd772efda14802c5783a13cab48ea0cb","slc_056a033a1ad0b7afd500dfe7e0939d8637a3870623bc629675ff7de5f99ae074","slc_75b35ef489ca6349f588352529da4b4ebfe7039e39081ade723e86905768c435","slc_9a80daab3cf4fa8d0fd17e907687da174b23cdb7501236a438e6a311800b1e7a","slc_f5d0f3de1640c1e6678b089582724e8c667e26afe8f3d89330f3d9ac5da7a703"],"source_ids":["src_253310f6882c56479f769950b6b562c6"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors add tools in the local_agent/tools directory, register them in tool_definitions.ts, render their XML tag in DyadMarkdownParser.tsx, and can add E2E tests modeled on e2e-tests/local_agent*.spec.ts with tool-call fixtures.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4c65b4db85feb487fadaf1cf896b9e78c5694531131908bb1ee4bfa6eec7913f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"dyad-sh/dyad@0c8403662504 snapshot 73f45ce23df314b3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2cc4f677b5b5cf43bbac64cbf18bf282ab7bb33d743fe7c3d1ce50398855d13d","slc_7999516dca8a7b1b25c970273da45e16bb83f383a81574d73bb6415d301dc0ed","slc_844b1fe68011b77f39490644ee000c2c92b73e4e64817787a45fbf19791e4f79"],"source_ids":["src_52a90da7cbd75fea9519d0578ce94f4e"],"text":"By default each LLM request includes the entire codebase plus a system prompt instructing XML-like responses; Smart Context uses smaller models to filter important files, and agentic iterative search is avoided mainly for cost reasons.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5d803da96a1b00b2cc5d01f83b6d3de993dcd7a20a2b91c6d1d3877eda713fea","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"dyad-sh/dyad@0c8403662504 snapshot 73f45ce23df314b3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_af09ce1abc9d307c05940ee8d18425a528535fc348816f7794959cd18940b56b"],"source_ids":["src_253310f6882c56479f769950b6b562c6"],"text":"The local agent's core loop lives in src/pro/main/ipc/handlers/local_agent/local_agent_handler.ts, calling the LLM until it stops making tool calls or hits a per-turn maximum step count; tool_definitions.ts lists the agent's tools.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6c09f7f3268f9571d5ef067bd4b16aa0b7d99a7dda9b97b0f7b95ea7a8bde254","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"dyad-sh/dyad@0c8403662504 snapshot 73f45ce23df314b3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9c76eb3fa78732b8383b424ad598b13f9ede0a8578016e518eec4f745e88722f","slc_d1e68d7329d5628c6aad3d3f1897b7b236cc17e9c0a52c22e17fd98d42a473cd","slc_d5968a00024fbad1ea94287e304729b2cd0ff475d900531123b59d6b4e3e7a3b"],"source_ids":["src_253310f6882c56479f769950b6b562c6","src_52a90da7cbd75fea9519d0578ce94f4e"],"text":"Dyad historically simulated tool calling with custom XML-like tags instead of models' formal tool calling, citing the ability to batch many calls and evidence that JSON code output hurts quality; a newer agent architecture moves toward standard tool calling.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7a4359e0ce5debf9d1744e4fa427e19066036f4b785f2750d248c7595fe1f42c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"dyad-sh/dyad@0c8403662504 snapshot 73f45ce23df314b3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7999516dca8a7b1b25c970273da45e16bb83f383a81574d73bb6415d301dc0ed","slc_b6077171d6ea94524d0a441c3d76635e93b69d8b9f91e6683ab812be8c9acf0e"],"source_ids":["src_52a90da7cbd75fea9519d0578ce94f4e"],"text":"The LLM responds with <dyad-*> tags (e.g. <dyad-write path=...>) that a specialized Markdown parser renders in the UI, and a response processor in the main process applies after user approval—writing or deleting files, adding NPM packages, etc.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9229067de4508db47853798c2b748aa1d4e0659b732b217895fe52767ae25398","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"dyad-sh/dyad@0c8403662504 snapshot 73f45ce23df314b3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c349a6ffd7aa6f5f19ff3558791e459042be9e4be43cc4eff8f4ad81be24bf8a"],"source_ids":["src_36b1ce03dad55f99a65722d832fa42f5"],"text":"The primary users are non-technical builders with no coding background running Dyad locally on Mac or Windows; a secondary audience brings their own API keys and local models.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_97b65571e0a43b62007d14db24bf4efe2de8432d59c674d4fd10addef21a9a36","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"dyad-sh/dyad@0c8403662504 snapshot 73f45ce23df314b3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_77801545a107f717bf43527f58b4166ccb4e1a71f31122f87909462d169c3080","slc_7e3730967c00d4d966db9e244d9fbe5c8b339c3fba770463b9fddfad176d81be","slc_e11987eede8c0c5c241d357cec6d0cd0ea8a6cf1c90bd496fcf0ace7476e1af9","slc_f1d95bd67425e1f4285c9eeb206e7af049f585c025a119756fe91866108c331c"],"source_ids":["src_25cf0d74e2615098b7e016f4f1d076e9","src_6086510952ea55a9bf328ec9f50cae91"],"text":"Repository development practice: English locale files are the source of truth, other locales must mirror their key structure with automatic English fallback, and a CI check warns on missing keys; contributions fall under a CLA granting Dyad Tech, Inc. copyright and patent licenses.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9b3c91818d60f5530bbde12d7e4b1ad5c8a88965c585a1bc5edbd93204c5e575","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"dyad-sh/dyad@0c8403662504 snapshot 73f45ce23df314b3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1e647bb2c867d6b26ac3d29520e704090cd635b0e177efe855b9b4090f14bb4d"],"source_ids":["src_6086510952ea55a9bf328ec9f50cae91"],"text":"The product includes agent built-in tool permission settings with per-tool options: Ask, Always allow, and Never allow.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b09bc830f2a70cc6465620b593cf964c2e0fa59edf489ad8e23e7a38504202b2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"dyad-sh/dyad@0c8403662504 snapshot 73f45ce23df314b3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_60db8b76bba31fd04aa2bbbd0253c18790701163044c876344f871986fe3bb82","slc_7bd6683aba5d05434cd87531a04ddac1aff92e1652ff3966d2df9bb220c2da90"],"source_ids":["src_52a90da7cbd75fea9519d0578ce94f4e"],"text":"Dyad is an Electron app with a React renderer process (sandboxed) and a privileged Node.js main process that accesses the filesystem, communicating via IPC.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b0e4cd46aefc75a2605ffd866daf5a42f1aa0da8abfd4652d0eddd991cae5599","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"dyad-sh/dyad@0c8403662504 snapshot 73f45ce23df314b3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_70bfa127cad8dcfcba03b917909f561f0f50d88f4429218e627cbe32ae73b3a3","slc_ad55e248fc12b3ac581b6f830357d77128060a8d08e7c6379350da3c4ae23e82"],"source_ids":["src_52a90da7cbd75fea9519d0578ce94f4e"],"text":"Dyad deliberately keeps a simple agentic loop—usually a single AI request, with optional auto-fix of TypeScript compiler errors—to keep costs low compared to more agentic tools.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e82e778498dbe870ef3a7075d7f2118b79cbc920ccc1990e88bb611d4908286a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"dyad-sh/dyad@0c8403662504 snapshot 73f45ce23df314b3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_306e526417bd8a89c1527cbe6336a54b02c33135afc9ee9413d8a8f6815a68af","slc_6325baa4f93e34d840438498f47ab48a9a5f554e15cf27ca259b2e920217e452"],"source_ids":["src_36b1ce03dad55f99a65722d832fa42f5","src_9a5d244828145a4b93279988a67db069"],"text":"Dyad is a local, open-source AI app builder where users describe an app in plain language and the AI generates code with a live preview on their machine, with local-first operation as the core differentiator.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_fdcfbd7d59c5b1635f2773858dceaf4b5e18246abde4a3e1d7adf1f499c4986b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"dyad-sh/dyad@0c8403662504 snapshot 73f45ce23df314b3","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_065abdb5289a5075ac5c4df07f169d668a65a418eed9ceca9be4f68fedffa2ac","slc_8c3e16dad4817868e4a3cac0b00ee4c73925fe52dd5ce247bbb480acf3f56e24","slc_985c7fdf4c9fdc713f05325c9c05d52e425ac10482c6fb8cbe5271085811329c","slc_f5d30a2dfb74fc38d8000b5f62b020881bd16a08a30562c732ad0bbee18a6b94"],"source_ids":["src_6086510952ea55a9bf328ec9f50cae91"],"text":"The i18n design specifies react-i18next and i18next (installed via npm) for translations with bundled locale JSON and no HTTP backend, and notes date-fns as an existing dependency for locale-aware date formatting.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4a8727fb3d4b402c9a62f82ea905a2b7"}
